            "title": "AI boom seen lifting chipmaking equipment sales 9% to $126 billion in 2026",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "AMSTERDAM, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Sales of equipment used to make computer chip wafers \u200bwill rise about 9% to $126 billion \u200cin 2026 and a further 7.3% to $135 billion in \u200c2027, as chipmakers expand capacity for logic and memory chips used in artificial intelligence, industry group SEMI forecast on Tuesday.",
